// Title: Office application spawning a command shell or script host
// Data source table: DeviceProcessEvents
// What it detects: Word, Excel, PowerPoint or Outlook starting cmd.exe, PowerShell, a Windows Script
//   Host process or mshta.exe. Malicious documents (macros, DDE, embedded objects) commonly use this
//   parent and child pair to run the first stage of an attack after a user opens an attachment.
// Likely false positives: Legitimate macros and add-ins that shell out, such as finance workbooks or
//   document automation; some enterprise plug-ins; IT-authored templates.
// MITRE ATT&CK technique: T1204.002 User Execution: Malicious File (delivered via T1566.001 Phishing:
//   Spearphishing Attachment), executing through T1059.001 PowerShell or T1059.003 Windows Command Shell
// Tuning notes: This table comes from Microsoft Defender for Endpoint. In Sentinel (Defender XDR
//   connector) the time column is TimeGenerated; in the Defender portal's advanced hunting use Timestamp
//   instead. Build an exclusion list from the InitiatingProcessCommandLine of known-good macros after a
//   baseline period. Consider also enabling the Attack Surface Reduction rule that blocks Office
//   applications from creating child processes, then use this query to find what it would have blocked.
// Status: Written against the documented Defender XDR schema. Not yet run in a live Sentinel workspace.

let lookback = 1d;
let officeApps = dynamic(["winword.exe", "excel.exe", "powerpnt.exe", "outlook.exe"]);
let shells = dynamic(["cmd.exe", "powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe", "wscript.exe", "cscript.exe", "mshta.exe"]);
DeviceProcessEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~ (officeApps)
| where FileName in~ (shells)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    DeviceName,
    Account = strcat(AccountDomain, "\\", AccountName),
    ParentProcess = InitiatingProcessFileName,
    ParentCommandLine = InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    ChildProcess = FileName,
    ChildCommandLine = ProcessCommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc
